{"item_id": "feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/14/skapion-unveils-the-worlds-first-native-counter-swarm-defense-system/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=skapion-unveils-the-worlds-first-native-counter-swarm-defense-system", "version_id": "9a5e2a80b66d75d088ffdd8e6e05447563732c112353bad9e860b528c3434497", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Out of scope under the Relevance rule: a large-scale counter-swarm air-defense system is not competitor gear. The text is a company press release with claims such as 'above 97%' interception and 'significantly lower cost' that have no independent support, which the Unsupported claims and Credibility rules do not allow us to present as fact.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.ssusa.org/content/new-zerotech-trace-x-5-25x-56-mm-ffp-rmg-h-mrad-illuminated-riflescope/", "version_id": "991971daa85980e726ccb3fc4bd7d41e0396c188b527973e3c9901e208a8bd70", "decision": "defer", "reason": "In scope under Relevance as a riflescope, but the item is a product announcement close to a press release, and the NRA notes flag it as a manufacturer claim. Its specifications (34 MRAD elevation, 31.5 oz, 0.1-MRAD turrets) come from the manufacturer, and there is no independent test, reviewer, or practitioner field experience, so the Credibility and Unsupported claims rules point to deferral. The piece also cites a list price of $899 and a $749 website price, which is sales-adjacent, and the item does not show an affiliation with Vortex or another Mammoth sponsor. It could be reconsidered if independent field testing appears.", "piece_ids": []}
